&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Day-to-Day&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor alarms, including fire, door, and duress alarms, while answering routine and emergency calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor CCTV, to protect the building and assets, also to prevent or help stop any crime from occurring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to life safety incidents (medical emergencies, natural disasters) and dispatch security officers, ERT, police, fire, and EMS personnel as needed via phone and radio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage and handle situations of a sensitive nature and maintain company’s confidentiality and information security practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create dispatch records for each officer deployed during your shift, and initiate incident reports and work orders as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Emergency Response Team (ERT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Alert media to identify, analyze, and support all events and incidents that impact or potentially could impact operations, facilities, and employees globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot technical issues with security systems, including CCTV and access control, to ensure proper functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in projects related to the GSOC role, with responsibilities ranging from providing input and guidance to taking full ownership of initiatives based on individual expertise and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring live AB4 body camera footage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent; associate or bachelor&#39;s degree in security management, Criminal Justice, or a related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years of experience in security operations, law enforcement, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess a Remote Pilot Certificate (Part 107) &amp;amp;/or be able to possess within 120 days of hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security CCTV monitoring systems and protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple lines of communication and multitask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic proficiency with surveillance and alarm systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills for clear incident documentation and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a professional demeanor in all interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to maintain composure and professionalism in high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in Security Management, Criminal Justice, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in a GSOC, corporate security, or a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in incident response and crisis management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of physical security protocols and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical thinking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of global security challenges and cultural sensitivity for operating in diverse environments.&lt;/li&gt;
